    "One mutation shape (misanchor). This measures detection of errors of that shape, not of the distribution of mistakes a real reconciler makes.",
    "THREE MODELS: one forged the error by rewriting the reconciler's rationale to match a moved anchor, one audited it, one judged the audit. The forger is pinned to the model and effort the reconciler ran at, given no tools, and its output is checked mechanically for the tell (no line within tolerance of the true anchor; the injected line present). The forge is shown the real source at the destination, because without it the paragraph invents the line's contents and becomes checkably false about the FILE — a second and louder error than the misanchor, which would inflate recall. That bounds it; it does not make the injected error indistinguishable from a real one.",
    "The ruling is a model grading a model. The verbatim-quote requirement and the control bound how wrong it can be silently; they do not make it a mechanical measurement.",
    "false_alarms is the instrument's own error rate and is never subtracted from recall.",
    "Seeds are few enough that one seed is a large fraction of the result; no aggregate threshold is honest here, per AC 8 of the parent request."
